# Aster VPN — Cursor Compatibility Rules

Canonical agent instructions live in `AGENTS.md`. Before changing code, read:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `docs/00_agentic/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md`
3. `PROJECT_STATUS.md`
4. `docs/TODO.md`
5. `docs/00_agentic/AGENTIC_CODING_GUIDE.md`
6. Specs directly related to the task

Hard constraints:

- Optimize only the one-tap VPN core loop: connect, trustworthy status, recoverable failure, subscription reason.
- Keep SwiftUI UI/business logic out of the Packet Tunnel Extension.
- Treat Extension resources as constrained and verify memory/CPU on target devices; do not assume an unmeasured fixed budget.
- Never log traffic content, full node URLs, UUIDs, tokens, receipts, or personal data.
- Do not use display strings as connection state. Use an explicit, testable state model.
- Report work as planned, implemented, build-verified, device-verified, or release-verified.
- Simulator builds do not verify VPN traffic. NetworkExtension changes require signed device evidence.
- Update project configuration through `project.yml`, regenerate with `./setup.sh`, and verify the generated project.
- When evidence conflicts, current code/tests/runtime and active SSOT outrank old specs. Record unresolved conflicts instead of guessing.

